WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.860
In this video, you build a virtual private cloud with three subnets, one for each tier of an application: web, app, and database. Then you check that the tiers reach each other inside the VPC.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.980
Under Overlay Networks, open Virtual Private Cloud and select Create.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:24.770
Name the VPC demo-3tier. A VPC is a separate router, and its address space is isolated from every other VPC.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.120
Select Create.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.210
In the demo-3tier group, select Create Subnet to add the first tier.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.230
Name it demo-web.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:40.010
The web tier gets the CIDR block 10.230.1.0/24.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:50.380
As the provider, select the overlay network demo-web-net. Virtual machines attach to this network, and Kube-OVN gives them addresses from this subnet.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:56.020
The gateway, 10.230.1.1, is the VPC router's port in this subnet.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:01.080
Enable DHCP, so that virtual machines get their address and route automatically.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.420
Select Create.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.150
Add the app tier the same way,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.500
with the name demo-app, the CIDR block 10.230.2.0/24,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.780
the overlay network demo-app-net,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.840
the gateway 10.230.2.1,

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.040
and DHCP enabled.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.820
Then the database tier,

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.220
demo-db, with 10.230.3.0/24,

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.750
the overlay network demo-db-net,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.300
the gateway 10.230.3.1,

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.260
and DHCP.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:52.760
The demo-3tier VPC now lists its three subnets.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:02:04.930
To test the network, three small virtual machines were created with kubectl, one on each tier's overlay network. Each runs a small web service, on port 80, 8080, or 5432.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.970
demo-web got 10.230.1.10 in the web subnet,

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:14.920
and demo-db got 10.230.3.10 in the database subnet.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.830
Open the console of demo-web in WebVNC.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.200
Log in as sles, with the password that cloud-init set.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:36.070
Ping demo-db, and request the page on its port 5432.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:49.110
Both answer. Subnets in the same VPC route to each other through the VPC router, with no extra configuration. That is convenient, but every tier also reaches the database.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:56.871
One VPC now holds three subnets, and its router connects them. Next, you make the database subnet private.
